 stopped and watched as a famously buttoned-up (if obviously still passionate) film-maker attempted some spontaneity with no danger of follow-up questions (or obligation to follow-up answers). From this, there is admittedly plenty of information to be gleaned: he has no designs on retiring, Tarantino-style. He will not make another superhero movie or a TV show. Heâ€™s fine with people watching movies on their phones or laptops. He will neither confirm nor deny that Interstellar is his favorite of his films. He will also neither confirm nor deny that he would like to make a Star Wars movie. (Perhaps the most intriguing, given that youâ€™d rather expect that to be a firm â€œnoâ€.)</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/jul/20/hollywood-press-tours-gimmicky">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;NQ-pYn0hgWhob3UsoYmR8SZSRWbzDCVhoFzNm1IToxMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;ACuAb0MI1RG73g1NnXQaqyla1-IzEFPXuzKVRrb_Y08ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;7yjq1OSQUxWM4oqIg_44IcjaFvKfF0MM774N-JjcLJoƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;C_f6Jl1n6Qk0iQSg04wc6uU6opW9sKmrEfgRUgLLG3sƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;tjzn6Ta6G57Ws2tgZNlBezRfpn6LyQDvD8JMK_qcEIwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ua36WbCNL3PdvKzdhnZFD7oPSC01wXzHXvr_imoEOD0ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;SQj5GHr9OTStAGoXPOX-VRGMK8Ce1b1fG1wxa_vidDsƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdst